@startuml
[*] --> IDLE

IDLE --> INITIATED : Initiation

INITIATED --> ESTABLISHED : Acceptance
INITIATED --> TERMINATED : Rejection
INITIATED --> HOLD : Wait / waiting
INITIATED --> IDLE : Timeout

ESTABLISHED --> HOLD : Hold / media
HOLD --> ESTABLISHED : Acceptance [waiting]
HOLD --> ESTABLISHED : Resume [media]

ESTABLISHED --> TERMINATED : Finish
HOLD --> TERMINATED : Finish / Rejection / Timeout

TERMINATED --> IDLE : Cleanup / invalidate handle

note right of HOLD
  HOLD is a business state with a reason:
  - waiting: pre-establishment wait
    (FIFO or promoted pending acceptance)
  - media: established call placed on hold
end note

note right of IDLE
  A transition to IDLE publishes any required
  terminal event first, then immediately releases
  the logical slot. No terminal-retention timer.
end note
@enduml
